# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# This roster runs entirely on OAuth subscriptions, not API keys:
#   anthropic/claude-sonnet-5       Claude Pro/Max   -> `pi` then /login -> Claude Pro/Max
#   openai-codex/gpt-6-astra        ChatGPT Plus/Pro -> `pi` then /login -> ChatGPT Plus/Pro (Codex)
#   (provider is "openai-codex", not "openai" — confirmed via `pi --list-models`)
#
# Both tokens land in ~/.pi/agent/auth.json, which pi checks before any
# environment variable (see resolution order in pi's docs/providers.md), so no
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY is ever read for these two agents.
#
# Confirm the exact registered model ids after logging in:
#   pi --list-models
# and update the `model:` lines in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml if they
# differ from the placeholders above.
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a model is
# written as provider/id, not that the provider is authenticated, so a missing
# login shows up when that agent runs, not at startup.

# Optional overrides
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
